Here's a practical C# approach to read Iranian license plates from images using OCR:

```csharp
using System;
using System.IO;
using Tesseract;
using OpenCvSharp;

class IranianLicensePlateReader
{
    static void Main(string[] args)
    {
        string imagePath = "plate_image.jpg";
        string outputFile = "plate_output.txt";

        // Load and preprocess image
        using var src = Cv2.ImRead(imagePath);
        using var gray = new Mat();
        Cv2.CvtColor(src, gray, ColorConversionCodes.BGR2GRAY);

        // Apply threshold for better OCR
        using var thresh = new Mat();
        Cv2.Threshold(gray, thresh, 0, 255, 
            ThresholdTypes.Binary | ThresholdTypes.Otsu);

        // Save preprocessed image temporarily
        string tempPath = "temp_processed.png";
        Cv2.ImWrite(tempPath, thresh);

        // OCR with Tesseract (Persian/Farsi)
        using var engine = new TesseractEngine("./tessdata", "fas", EngineMode.Default);
        using var img = Pix.LoadFromFile(tempPath);
        using var page = engine.Process(img);

        string plateText = page.GetText().Trim();

        // Write to file
        File.WriteAllText(outputFile, plateText);
        Console.WriteLine($"Plate detected: {plateText}");

        // Cleanup
        File.Delete(tempPath);
    }
}
```

**Required NuGet Packages:**
- `Tesseract` (OCR engine)
- `OpenCvSharp4` (image processing)

**Setup Notes:**
1. Download Persian trained data (`fas.traineddata`) from Tesseract GitHub
2. Place in `./tessdata` folder
3. Iranian plates use Persian numerals—ensure proper font support

